.TH USBRADIOPLUS 7 "August 2026" "USBRadioPlus alpha" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
usbradioplus \- enhanced USB radio channel driver for AllStarLink
.SH DESCRIPTION
USBRadioPlus is an Asterisk channel driver for CM108-, CM109-, and CM119-family
USB radio interfaces.  It replaces
.BR chan_usbradio
for stations that need more configurable audio filtering and optional dynamics
processing.  Radio signaling, USB mixer control, PTT, carrier-operated squelch,
CTCSS, and tuning are provided in the same channel driver.
.PP
Each configured interface appears to Asterisk as
.BR RadioPlus/ name .
Channel and hardware settings are read from
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5).
Optional audio-processing graphs are read from
.BR usbradioplus-processing.conf (5).
.SH INSTALLATION
Install the matching ASL3 Asterisk development package and the DSP development
libraries, then build, test, and install with:
.PP
.nf
make
make check
sudo make prefix=/usr install
.fi
.PP
For a release archive on an ASL3 node, the supported convenience command is:
.PP
.nf
sudo ./install.sh
.fi
.PP
The convenience installer obtains the required Debian build packages, builds
the module and utilities, runs the hardware-independent tests, and installs the
result.  Installation does not load a module, restart Asterisk, or edit an
Asterisk configuration file.
.SH ACTIVATION
Retain the installed
.B chan_usbradio.so
and its configuration until USBRadioPlus has been tested on the radio system.
Do not allow both drivers to open the same USB interface.
.PP
In
.BR /etc/asterisk/modules.conf ,
prevent the old driver from loading and load USBRadioPlus.  For example:
.PP
.nf
noload => chan_usbradio.so
load => chan_usbradioplus.so
.fi
.PP
Copy or rename the working channel configuration to
.BR /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf .
Review it using
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5).
.PP
In the applicable node section of
.BR /etc/asterisk/rpt.conf ,
change only the channel technology in
.BR rxchannel .
Keep the device name and the remaining channel arguments unchanged.  For
example:
.PP
.nf
rxchannel = RadioPlus/usb
.fi
.PP
During a maintenance window, restart Asterisk, then verify PTT, COS, CTCSS,
receive audio, transmit deviation, and duplex operation before returning the
station to service.  Do not replace a running module with
.B module reload;
on some ASL3 systems the CM119 remains unassigned until Asterisk restarts.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The channel file contains hardware selection, radio signaling, audio routing,
filters, levels, delays, duplex operation, and GPIO assignments.  See
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5)
for every option, accepted value, and default.
.PP
The processing file contains the local-receiver, link, and transmitter audio
graphs.  See
.BR usbradioplus-processing.conf (5)
for graph order, processing controls, limits, and defaults.
.SH TUNING UTILITIES
.TP
.B usbradioplus-tune
Interactive, keyboard-operated setup for USB mixer levels, receive voice and
CTCSS levels, squelch, transmit voice and CTCSS deviation, PTT, test tone,
statistics, and EEPROM storage.
.TP
.B usbradioplus-rxlevel
Receive-level calibration and monitoring, including peak, RMS, and clipping
information.
.TP
.B usbradioplus-processing-tune
Checks and edits the optional processing graphs and can display live processing
statistics.
.PP
See
.BR usbradioplus-tune (8)
for operating instructions and the service-monitor procedure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/<multiarch>/asterisk/modules/chan_usbradioplus.so
Asterisk channel module.
.TP
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus.conf
Channel, radio-interface, and tuning configuration.
.TP
.B /etc/asterisk/usbradioplus-processing.conf
Optional audio-processing configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR usbradioplus.conf (5),
.BR usbradioplus-processing.conf (5),
.BR usbradioplus-tune (8),
.BR modules.conf (5),
.BR rpt.conf (5)
